eates  tv shows like the arrowverse you know um  the flash series and all these things  superman versus lowest at the moment and  superman versus lowe's like they're in a  fight well they are married but um  superman and lois um back in the day um  smallville they always have reasonable  production value and decent budgets  without you know maybe being massive  um but they do produce some really  interesting and sometimes very brave  television i'm thinking like the series  i zombie very clever tv show very not  really normal for a kind of a network  television show um but very brave very  creative this is a tv network that i  think will allow jms to have the  show that he wants to do and obviously  jms has had a very successful career  including babylon 5 and since  he has enough gravitas and enough  respect within the cw network that i  think they're going to let him do what  he wants without having too much  interference we're going to actually see  the babylon 5 jms envisages on our  screens  but how about the tv show itself now he  has obviously said this is going to be a  bottom up hard reboot it's not going to  be the babylon 5 group grew up with but  i think at its core there will be  certain parts that will be for example  the babylon 5 station still seems to be  a 5 mile long beacon in space space  station in the neutral zone with several  different species coming and going a  haven for smugglers and traffic and  explorers and everything else so that  will still be very much i imagine  similar or at least  something that we can recognize  but the tv show itself is going to be  very different he talks about how  babylon 5 reflected the culture and the  problems society back in the 90s and he  wants the new tv show to do exactly the  same but time has moved on we're talking  nearly 30 years  we do still have fractions in our  society we have friction within our  political systems we have a very diverse  society in a very fractured society he  wants the new bible babylon 5 to still  reflect that so we're still going to be  talking about some of the things like  freedom and things like that that we see  in babylon 5 from the original but in a  very different way  he's also though hinted what the  storyline is going to roughly be in the  new first series it's going to be still  based around captain sheridan bruce  broxlander's character from the first  series  he's going to be coming to the station  as its new captain  he is going to have some sort of  mysterious background which he kind of  hinted at in the first series as well  but i think this is going to go far more  into it  but as he arrives a earth company  accidentally triggers a conflict with a  species that they know very little about  and that might be anything up to a  million years ahead of them in  technology this is going to put babylon  5 at the front line of this conflict and  basically mean that they are the best  line of defense for earth's survival  who this enemy is going to be this is  not 100 clear because obviously we have  the conflict between the mimbari and  earth and the sheridan character was  right in the middle of that conflict  is we got are we going to see a repeat  of that or is that going to be something  that is sidelined because the conflict  with the shadows is going to be maybe  developed in a slightly different way  now this was always a species that sort  of had come from ancient times and had  been awoken to return to scourge through  the galaxy is this something that is  going to be maybe woken by earth  interference something that this earth  company does that triggers the conflict  or are we going to see the mumbari war  but in far more detail than we ever did  in the series and potentially delivered  a different way  either way i'm absolutely certain jms is  going to do a stunning job and this is  the one series in 2022 i'm most excited  about amazon can spend a billion quid on  lord of the rings  i'll take it or leave it  but babylon 5 returning to our screens  now that is something i am genuinely  excited about and i'm absolutely  convinced we're going to see lots of  twists and turns just like that in a  completely new series with a completely  new look  i can't wait i'm really excited  so if you are new to the channel please  like subscribe hit that bell  notification share it wherever you like  do all that stuff um go on facebook  we're on there there's a link in the  description we're also on twitter  there's a link there too  please guys tell me what you think in  the comments about the return of babylon  5 what sort of series would you like to  see what stories would you like to see  tackled are we afraid that this series  might get ruined like so many others and  become some woke nonsense  i very much doubt that though i don't  think jms would allow that nonsense to  go on but you know it's always a risk  so tell me what you think please i can't  wait to read your comments  as always please stay safe and i'll see  you next time

